cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Nutrition_microbiome_reproducibility: reproduction of the figures of
  "Sugar-rich foods exacerbate antibiotic-induced microbiome disruption"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
  The accompanying article is published in Nature
  (https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-026-11077-3); please cite the article in preference to the software.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dai
    given-names: Anqi
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3106-4624"
    affiliation: >-
      Adult Bone Marrow Transplantation Service, Department of Medicine,
      Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center, New York, NY, USA
repository-code: "https://github.com/Anqi-Dai/Nutrition_microbiome_reproducibility"
abstract: >-
  This repository facilitates reproduction of the figures from the manuscript
  "Sugar-rich foods exacerbate antibiotic-induced microbiome disruption",
  built from a small set of de-identified released tables. Every panel is rebuilt by a numbered R script that reads only from
  released_data/ and writes one PDF per panel. Scripts are organised by analysis
  family: expensive Bayesian models are fit once and cached, then consumed by the
  panels that need them. The inputs needed for figure generation are available,
  including de-identified patient-level clinical-outcome and medication tables.
keywords:
  - microbiome
  - diet
  - dietary sugar
  - antibiotics
  - hematopoietic cell transplantation
  - reproducibility
  - R
license: MIT
version: 1.2.0
date-released: "2026-08-25"
